From a0b6dcefe17cea1b47d95319ace361b79f57d106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Praveen Talari <quic_ptalari@quicinc.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jul 2024 19:28:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PENDING: serial: qcom-geni: Enable Serial on SA8255p platform

Enable or disable resources such as clocks, interconnect
paths, and TLMM (GPIOs) via the logical power domain,
invoked as part of geni_spi_transition_d3d0 where d0 is on
and d3 is off states.

The bandrate is handle through perf domain with help
of perf levels and we are directly passing baudrate value
as perf level using dev_pm_opp_set_level().

Change-Id: Ide3e59ccb35baf674cd45a75e903be4c0e97979e
Signed-off-by: Praveen Talari <quic_ptalari@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Nikunj Kela <quic_nkela@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Shazad Hussain <quic_shazhuss@quicinc.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c | 311 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 238 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
